This file is deliberately explicit rather than absent. A public
repository without a license file is "all rights reserved" by default,
and readers are left guessing. So, plainly:

  You may read this repository.
  You may not copy, modify, redistribute or build on it
  until an open-source license replaces this file.

Sebastian Schulz holds the copyright in this work, including the
framework design -- the field set, the comparison rules, the stage
ladder and the non-equations -- and the source code implementing it.

To open this up, replace this file with the chosen license text and
keep the copyright line above. A license grants permissions; it does
not transfer ownership. The author remains the rights holder either
way.
